   "prompt": "<p>A table <code>people(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT, city TEXT, age INTEGER)</code> (Lesson 5) serves four queries, run with different values in place of each <code>?</code>:</p>\n<pre data-label=\"SQL\"><code>-- Q1\nSELECT * FROM people WHERE name = ?\n-- Q2\nSELECT name FROM people WHERE city = ? AND age BETWEEN ? AND ?\n-- Q3\nSELECT * FROM people WHERE city = ? ORDER BY age\n-- Q4\nSELECT COUNT(*) FROM people WHERE age &gt; ?</code></pre>\n<p>Set <code>INDEXES</code> to a list of at most three <code>CREATE INDEX</code> statements such that SQLite's <code>EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN</code> shows: no query scanning the table (no <code>SCAN people</code> step); Q2 and Q4 using a <em>covering</em> index; and Q3 needing no separate sort (no <code>USE TEMP B-TREE FOR ORDER BY</code> step).</p>",
